/-!
# Cryptarchia certificates

Numeric instances of the settlement theorem at the specification's parameters,
generated by `tools/certgen`. The automaton tables are checked by kernel evaluation over `ℚ`
(`Cryptarchia/Prob/AutoQ.lean`), the remaining numbers by `norm_num`; building each
certificate takes about 40 s (`lake build CryptarchiaCerts`).

Each `certified_tsi` bounds a finality violation by the settlement bound, plus the
estimate's band, plus the canonical prefixes' consistency epoch by epoch
(`final_bimm_ro_tsi6`):

* `E20D11` — every epoch for a year (49 epochs) at β = 0.2, Δ = 11 slots, k = 2160, with
  full withholding: `1e-9 + 49 · 4.2e-16 + 49 · 1e-9 ≈ 5.0e-8`.
* `E20D11M2` — the same parameters over two months (slot 5184000, 9 epochs):
  `1e-10 + 9 · 4.2e-16 + 9 · 1e-10 ≈ 1.0e-9`.

Other configurations can be generated with `tools/certgen` (see its README).
-/

